From 76ddb10781c4318ff97e17ea039b02efda60a180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:55:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VR hands and finger tracking, battle table review fixes, HD
 battle HUD, display defaults

- VR hands: a smooth hand mesh (1800 triangles, three poses) blended from the
  trigger and grip, skinned to XR_EXT_hand_tracking's 26 joints where fingers
  are tracked (ga2_vr_hand.h); "VR finger tracking" setting.
- Battle table: the game decides every press (select, re-select, order),
  paced by game frames; drags arm on movement; tracking loss cancels; units
  off the plate are not picked; hover hysteresis and one owner; team colours,
  a selection ring, an outcome-coloured order beam, a release flash; micro,
  small and big haptics with grab ticks; zoom about the hands' midpoint;
  both grips held still recentre; the HUD's pieces as panels around the table
  (no flat screen); guide titles in Title Case, consumed buttons masked,
  bare-hand timeouts; cheat menu drawn over the table.
- HD battle graphics (setting, default on at 2x/4x): the battle HUD per layer;
  flat-coloured art redrawn as shapes (ga2_flatart.h, rings as true circles),
  the rest with Anime4K; memory-budgeted result caches.
- Fixes: the Anime4K chain's surface pool recycles (upscaling stopped after a
  few sizes); pictures that keep changing (movie strips) stay native; the
  scene's 2D/3D change re-decides textures.
- Display: internal resolution "auto" (4x from 1200 lines, 2x below; 2x in VR
  and on ARM), borderless fullscreen and the screen's own shape by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
